5	## Branching Workflow
6	
7	Multiple paths based on conditions:
8	
9	```dy
10	machine "Conditional Workflow"
11	
12	Task evaluate "Evaluate condition";
13	Task pathA "Process path A";
14	Task pathB "Process path B";
15	Task merge "Merge results";
16	
17	evaluate -> pathA, pathB;
18	pathA -> merge;
19	pathB -> merge;
20	```
21	
22	Pattern notes:
23	- `evaluate -> pathA, pathB` creates edges to multiple targets
24	- Both paths converge at `merge`
25	- Useful for parallel processing or conditional execution
26	
27	## Sequential Processing
28	
29	Data processing pipeline:
30	
31	```dy
32	machine "Data Pipeline"
33	
34	Task fetch "Fetch data" {
35	    source: "api";
36	    endpoint: "https://api.example.com/data";
37	};
38	
39	Task transform "Transform data" {
40	    operations: ["filter", "map", "reduce"];
41	};
42	
43	Task validate "Validate results" {
44	    schema: #validationSchema;
45	};
46	
47	Task store "Store results" {
48	    destination: "database";
49	};
50	
51	fetch -> transform -> validate -> store;
52	```
53	
54	Pipeline characteristics:
55	- Linear flow: each step depends on the previous
56	- Attributes configure each step
57	- Schema references (`#validationSchema`) for validation
