5	## Basic LLM Task
6	
7	Simple LLM-powered task:
8	
9	```dy
10	machine "Text Analysis"
11	
12	Context config {
13	    model: "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022";
14	    temperature: 0.7;
15	};
16	
17	Task analyze {
18	    prompt: "Analyze the sentiment of the following text: {{ input.text }}";
19	};
20	
21	Input input {
22	    text: "I love this product!";
23	};
24	
25	Output result {
26	    sentiment: "TBD";
27	    confidence: 0.0;
28	};
29	
30	input -> analyze -> result;
31	```
32	
33	LLM basics:
34	- `Context` node configures model and parameters
35	- `prompt` attribute contains the LLM instruction
36	- Template syntax `{{ input.text }}` injects input values
37	- Linear flow: input → task → output
38	
39	## Multi-Step Analysis
40	
41	Chain of LLM tasks:
42	
43	```dy
44	machine "Document Processing"
45	
46	Context llm {
47	    model: "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022";
48	};
49	
50	Input document {
51	    content: #documentContent;
52	};
53	
54	Task extract {
55	    prompt: "Extract key entities from: {{ document.content }}";
56	};
57	
58	Task classify {
59	    prompt: "Classify the document based on entities: {{ extract.result }}";
60	};
61	
62	Task summarize {
63	    prompt: "Summarize the document: {{ document.content }}";
64	};
65	
66	Task combine {
67	    prompt: "Combine classification and summary: {{ classify.result }} + {{ summarize.result }}";
68	};
69	
70	document -> extract -> classify -> combine;
71	document -> summarize -> combine;
72	```
73	
74	Multi-step patterns:
75	- Sequential: `extract -> classify`
76	- Parallel: both `classify` and `summarize` feed into `combine`
77	- Reference previous task results: `{{ extract.result }}`
78	- Multiple paths from same input
